; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Ferris Wheel
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     animation, rotation, SIN, COS, gondolas, CLEAN
; SUMMARY:  A fairground Ferris wheel turns slowly, and its gondolas always hang straight down.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A big wheel with spokes stands on two legs at an evening fair.
;   Eight colored gondolas hang from the rim. As the wheel turns,
;   the gondolas travel round with it but stay upright, because
;   they hang from a pin and gravity keeps them level. Lights on the
;   rim twinkle as they go.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Press Stop to end it. Change :speed at the bottom.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * points on a circle with SIN and COS
;   * the difference between turning a shape and moving it round:
;     the spokes turn, the gondolas only move
;   * a frame counter driving the whole animation
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the gondolas swing a little with SIN of the time.
;   * Add more gondolas: 12 instead of 8.
;   * Make the lights change color as the wheel turns.
; ============================================================

make "colors [[230 70 70] [250 170 40] [240 220 60] [80 190 100]
              [60 160 230] [120 100 220] [220 90 200] [250 130 130]]

; RIM.POINT outputs the point on the rim at :angle around (0, 40).
to rim.point :angle :r
  output list :r * sin :angle 40 + :r * cos :angle
end

; FRAMEWORK draws the legs, the rim and the spokes at angle :turn.
to framework :turn
  setpencolor [90 90 110] setpensize 8
  penup setxy 0 40 pendown setxy -150 -260
  penup setxy 0 40 pendown setxy 150 -260
  setpencolor [180 180 200] setpensize 4
  ; ARC draws a circle around the turtle, so stand on the hub
  penup setxy 0 40 pendown arc 360 200
  setpensize 2
  for [k 0 7] [
    penup setxy 0 40 pendown
    setpos rim.point :turn + 45 * :k 200
  ]
  setpencolor [90 90 110] setpensize 24 dot [0 40]
end

; GONDOLA hangs one gondola from the rim point at :angle. It hangs
; straight down whatever the angle is: we only move it, never turn it.
to gondola :angle :color
  localmake "pin rim.point :angle 200
  localmake "x first :pin
  localmake "y last :pin
  setpencolor [60 60 70] setpensize 2
  penup setpos :pin pendown setxy :x :y - 18
  ; the cabin is a thick short line with round ends
  setpencolor :color setpensize 26
  penup setxy :x - 8 :y - 32 pendown setxy :x + 8 :y - 32
  ; the rim light at the pin
  setpencolor pick [[255 240 150] [255 255 255]]
  setpensize 8 dot :pin
end

; FRAME draws everything with the wheel turned :turn degrees.
to frame :turn
  clean
  framework :turn
  for [k 0 7] [gondola :turn + 45 * :k item :k + 1 :colors]
  ; the ground
  setpencolor [40 50 40] setpensize 60
  penup setxy -400 -280 setheading 90 pendown forward 800
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [40 50 90]
make "speed 0.6
make "turn 0
forever [
  frame :turn
  make "turn :turn + :speed
  wait 1
]
